<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clonakilty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clonakilty is a market town in West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cork">Cork</a>, Ireland, at the head of Clonakilty Bay on the Atlantic coast. It was developed as a plantation town in the early 17th century by Richard Boyle, 1st Earl of Cork, and received a royal charter in 1613. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-collins">Michael Collins</a>, the Irish revolutionary leader, was born nearby at Woodfield in 1890.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clonakilty.jpg" alt="Clonakilty" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chmee2 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clonakilty2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
